					Theoc.
					2.120
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.64
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ μὴ φυλάσσεις μίκρ᾽, ἀπολεῖς τὰ
					μείζονα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Mon.</u>
					172
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθάνατον ἔχθραν μὴ
			φύλαττε</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>: with a predic. added, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. τινά δεδεμένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					5.47
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδέκαστον φ. τὴν διάνοιαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Th.</u>
					34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκύμααντον τὸ πέλαγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DMar.</u>
					5.1
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσος παρ᾽ ὑμῖν ὁ φθόνος
				φυλάττεται</span>
			<i>is fostered</i> by . . , <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				382
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>keep in</i> a place, <i>continue in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόδε δῶμα φυλάσσοις, ἀθάνατός τ᾽
					εἴης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.208
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>notice, observe,</i> Ath.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<i>maintain, hold fast to</i> a view, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ σπουδαῖον εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
